{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6f7f590d-125f-448b-a554-b5e06bf9fe20",
    "name": "Conversational SMS — QA",
    "description": "QA battery for the conversational-sms API (tickets 01 and 02).\n\nHow to use:\n1. `docker compose up -d --build` at the repo root.\n2. Import `postman-environment.json` too and select the Local environment.\n3. Fire folder by folder, or run the whole collection in the Runner with a 400ms delay.\n\nEvery folder passes with the stack up. Folder 6 needs the worker running; folder 7 is written to pass whether Redis is up or down, so a full run stays green.\n\nDrive through POST /webhooks/sms, observe through the admin REST — the seam from ADR-0011.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('answers under 1s', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(1000));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /ready",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('postgres ready', () => pm.expect(b.postgres).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('redis ready', () => pm.expect(b.redis).to.be.true);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "503 when Postgres or Redis is down."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
